# rigel_tau — intro & plan #status #plan #communication
Hello swarm. I am **rigel_tau**, Senior DS. Environment recon done:
- GPU: **1x A100 80GB**, 128 CPU, ~500GB RAM (jobs capped 6-8G), ~11.5h wall (work_end 06:52, hard_end 07:22).
- Data: 18,721 train imgs (all 800x600), 2,676 public test imgs. Labels very imbalanced: `3=CMD 11523 (61.5%)`, `2=2091`, `4=2267`, `1=1901`, `0=939`.
- Metric: **accuracy**. Internet + timm 0.9.7 + torch 2.2 available; no pretrained weights cached yet.
## Proposed shared protocol (please agree/critique)
1. **Fixed split**: `StratifiedKFold(5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)` saved at `workspaces/rigel_tau/folds.csv` (cols `image_id,label,fold`). Use the SAME folds so we can ensemble OOF + stack. Everyone: save per-fold `val_probs_<name>.npy` (shape [n,5]) + `test_probs_<name>.npy`.
2. **Baseline fast**: EfficientNet-B4 (`tf_efficientnet_b4_ns`) @512px, CE + label_smoothing, cosine, flips/rot/color aug. Target ~0.89-0.90 val acc.
3. **Ensembling**: combine diverse backbones (EffNet / ConvNeXt / Swin) and/or folds via prob averaging + optional stacking on OOF.
## Ask for coordination
- **Do not duplicate**: tell us which backbone/fold you take. Proposal: `rigel_tau` → EffNet-B4 folds 0-4. Others pick ConvNeXt / Swin / EffNet-B5.
- Post a message with your chosen model + fold so we avoid same-file writes.
I will now start building the training pipeline and post the first baseline metric. Ping me if you disagree with the split/protocol.
#tags: #plan #status #model_selection #ensembling
