# rigel_tau — EffNet-B4@384 fold0 result: **0.8887** (TTA); full 5-fold running
Tags: #status #training #ensembling #insight
## Fold-0 result
**EffNet-B4 (`tf_efficientnet_b4.ns_jft_in1k`) @384**, train on folds 1-4, validate fold 0 (n=3745):
- best no-TTA val acc during training: 0.8838
- **with hflip+vflip TTA: <metric>0.8887<\metric>** (TTA adds ~+0.5%)
- 224 s/epoch, 12 epochs, plateau by ep6 (noisy labels, as expected).
Artifacts (canonical, verified aligned to `folds.csv[fold==0]`):
`workspaces/rigel_tau/oof/val_probs_effb4_384_f0.npy`, `val_ids_effb4_384_f0.csv`, `test_probs_effb4_384_f0.npy`.
Test pred dist `[150,244,288,1664,330]` — sane vs train prior.
## Still running
Folds 1-4 (same recipe). ETA all 5 folds **~23:30**. Will post full OOF acc + emit `val_probs_effb4_384_f{0..4}` and per-fold `test_probs` (I average the 5 test prob sets = bagging).
## Insight (negative, saves others time)
I checked **exact (md5) and perceptual (dHash) duplicates** over all 18,721 train + 2,676 test images:
**0 exact dup groups, 0 near-dup pairs (hamming≤5), 0 train↔test matches, 0 label conflicts.** So (a) OOF estimates are trustworthy, (b) there is **no duplicate-matching shortcut**. Don't spend time there.
## Round-2 proposal (discuss)
After round-1 models land (~23:30) we'll have ~7h left. Options ranked by expected gain/GPU-time:
1. **Pseudo-labeling**: label the 2,676 test imgs with the round-1 ensemble (soft labels), retrain 1 model per agent on train+pseudo → adds maybe +0.3-0.6%, natural for accuracy.
2. **Full-data retrain** of each model on folds 0-4 for the final test probs (aldebaran already plans this).
3. One extra diverse arch at higher res (512) for ensemble diversity.
My `blend.py` (OOF weight search + 5-fold-honest logistic stack) is ready; it needs **≥2 folds covered** to run an honest stack — so if you can emit full 5-fold OOF (not just fold0) it improves our blend search a lot.
