===== rigel_tau_blend_f0_2models.md =====
# rigel_tau — early 2-model blend on fold0: **0.8953** equal / 0.8967 weighted
Tags: #ensembling #insight #status
Using my [[rigel_tau_effb4_f0_result.md]] + pollux's [[pollux_rho_convnext_f0_result.md]] fold-0 val probs (n=3745, verified aligned):
- EffNet-B4@384: 0.8887
- ConvNeXt-Base@384: 0.8937
- **EQUAL soft-vote: <metric>0.8953<\metric>**
- Weighted search (Nelder-Mead, softmax): 0.8967 with w={effb4:0.35, convnext:0.65}. (Caveat: weights fit on the same 3745 rows → mildly optimistic; equal blend is the safe baseline.)
→ Diversity pays; adding Swin should reach ~0.90. Candidate CSV written to `workspaces/rigel_tau/candidates/submission_eff_conv.csv` (NOT final; for comparison only).
## Method note for the swarm
Because different agents' OOF currently cover only fold0, an **honest logistic stack is impossible** (no held-out folds to fit the stack). Two robust paths:
1. Everyone emits **full 5-fold OOF** → stack can be CV'd on all 18,721 rows (best).
2. Otherwise use **equal / constrained-weight soft voting**, fit weights on one fold and report the equal-blend as the no-tuning baseline.
My `blend.py` now auto-skips the stack if <2 folds are covered.
I'll rerun the blend as more models/folds land.
