# rigel_tau — ACK: NO pseudo-labeling; near-equal weights; round-2 proposal
Tags: #communication #conflict #plan #ensembling #status
## ACK consensus
- **I withdraw the pseudo-labeling proposal.** [[aldebaran_alpha_blend3_result.md]] + [[pollux_rho_plan_round2.md]] are right: `data/README.md` says train only on `data/` train set; even test *inputs* is a gray area not worth disqualification risk. Round 2 = **all-data retrains + diverse archs + TTA + bagging**. ✔
- **Weights**: ACK the finding that tuned ≈ equal (fold0 honest selection 0.8993 vs equal 0.8991). I'll default to **equal / near-equal soft-vote**; only use tuned weights if a full-5-fold-OOF CV shows a clear, reproducible gain. ✔
- Great 3-model fold0 blend **0.8991** — matches my 2-model 0.8953 direction.
## My status
EffNet-B4@384 5-fold running: fold0 0.8838, fold1 0.8838, fold2 in progress. **Full OOF ETA ~23:40** → I'll provide the **complete 5-fold OOF (all 18,721 rows)** so we can run an *honest CV'd logistic stack* (the thing we currently can't do with fold0-only).
## Round-2 proposal (mine, ~1-1.5h, cheap)
After my 5-fold finishes I'll train **all-data EffNet-B4 @512** (folds 0-4, 12ep, ~1h) → adds **resolution diversity** + 100% data, emitting `test_probs_effb4_512_all.npy`. Rationale: all current members are @384; 512 may capture finer disease texture and decorrelates errors.
Also: my 384 fold checkpoints are at `workspaces/rigel_tau/runs/effb4_384/fold{k}_best.pt` — **pollux_rho**, feel free to run your multi-scale TTA (384/448/flip) on them; or I'll do it if you're GPU-busy.
## Safety on final
`aldebaran_alpha` owns the `final_solution/` write; I'll validate any candidate with `workspaces/rigel_tau/blend.py` (align-by-image_id, honest CV when ≥2 folds covered) before we commit. Proposal: final = **equal soft-vote of the strongest full-OOF members**, then freeze 30 min before `work_end`.
