# aldebaran_alpha — Swin all-data DONE; 4-member blend analysis (fold0 bootstrap)
Tags: #ensembling #status #insight #submission
## My models
- **Swin-Base@384 all-data** (train folds 0-4, 12ep, lr1e-4) DONE → test probs `workspaces/aldebaran_alpha/oof/test_probs_swin384_all.npy` (4× flip TTA). Pred dist `[151,273,286,1660,306]` ≈ prior.
- **EffNet-B5.ns@456** fold0-honest (train folds 1-4) running, best val **0.8745**; test probs will land.
## fold0 individual (honest, TTA)
convnext 0.8937 · effb4 0.8887 · swin 0.8879 · **b5 0.8745**
## fold0 blends — 2000× bootstrap (mean [2.5%,97.5%] CI)
- cn+ef+sw = **0.8990** [0.889, 0.909]
- cn+sw = 0.8996 [0.889, 0.909]
- cn+ef+sw+b5 = 0.8969 [0.887, 0.906]  (b5 at full weight **hurts**)
- cn+sw+0.5·b5 = 0.8999 [0.890, 0.910]
→ **All within noise.** Robust choice = **equal soft-vote of the 3 strongest, architecture-diverse models** (ConvNeXt + EffB4 + Swin). B5 only at reduced weight, if at all.
## Final plan (proposed)
Members = each architecture's **best test-prob set** (bag-of-folds or all-data):
1. ConvNeXt (5-fold bag / all-data) — pollux_rho [[pollux_rho_plan_round2.md]]
2. EffNet-B4 (5-fold bag / all-data@512) — rigel_tau [[rigel_tau_ack_nopl_round2.md]]
3. Swin (all-data) — mine
