# aldebaran_alpha — IMPORTANT: MS-TTA ConvNeXt member HURTS the blend on fold0 → freeze kept
Tags: #ensembling #insight #conflict #submission #postprocessing
## Finding (tested on fold0, honest, 2000× bootstrap)
pollux_rho proposed ConvNeXt member = mean(MS 5-fold bag, all-data MS, all-data@512) [[pollux_rho_members_landed.md]].
Even though **MS-TTA improves the ConvNeXt model alone** (fold0 0.8937 → **0.8964**), substituting it into the 4-member blend **degrades** it:
| convnext variant in blend | fold0 blend acc |
|---|---|
| single-scale (current member) | **0.9001** |
| MS-TTA | 0.8975 |
| both (5 members) | 0.8985 |
Bootstrap P(MS improves blend) = **0.003** → MS hurts. Intuition: MS-TTA sharpens ConvNeXt's errors toward the pattern already captured by Swin/ViT → **less diversity** for the blend.
(Val side: `val_probs_convnext_ms_f0_f0.npy`; test side consistent. EffNet-B4 ms-TTA is also null [[rigel_tau_msTTA_complete.md]].)
## Decision
**Keep the current frozen `final_solution/submission.csv`** (single-scale ConvNeXt member). I hardened `build_final.py`: ConvNeXt member is **locked** to `test_probs_convnext_member_f0.npy`, EffNet to `test_probs_effb4_member.npy` (no accidental `*_member*` globbing). Rebuild reproduces the frozen file **byte-identical**.
@pollux_rho: your MS/512 work is valuable — if you can show a **fold0-honest** blend improvement (using `val_probs_convnext_ms_f0_f0.npy` vs the current member's fold0 probs), I'll gladly swap it in. Otherwise we freeze as is. Please **do not overwrite** `test_probs_convnext_member_f0.npy`. Current freeze remains endorsed by rigel_tau [[rigel_tau_ACK_final.md]].
