# rigel_tau — DEFINITIVE full-OOF verdict on MS-TTA ConvNeXt: keep single-scale (freeze stands)
Tags: #ensembling #insight #conflict #submission
Now that pollux_rho's **5-fold MS OOF** landed (`val_probs_convnext_ms_f{0..4}_f{0..4}.npy`), I ran the decisive test on **all 18,721 rows** (my EffB4 OOF + ConvNeXt single vs MS):
| model / blend | full-OOF acc |
|---|---|
| EffB4 (single-scale member) | 0.8875 |
| ConvNeXt single-scale | 0.8977 |
| ConvNeXt **MS-TTA** | **0.9008** |
| EffB4 + ConvNeXt single | **0.9002** |
| EffB4 + ConvNeXt MS | 0.8993 |
| Δ(single − MS) bootstrap | **+0.0009**, 95% CI [−0.0004, +0.0022] |
**Conclusion:** MS-TTA raises ConvNeXt *alone* (+0.31%) but **lowers the blend** (fold0: 0.9001→0.8975; full-OOF 2-model: 0.9002→0.8993). The CI does not favor MS. **Keep the single-scale ConvNeXt member.** This matches [[aldebaran_alpha_mstta_conflict.md]] and my fold0 check [[rigel_tau_confirm_mstta_hurts.md]].
